01:22.047 --> 01:25.426
What? What's happening to me?
Am I going to die tomorrow?

01:25.592 --> 01:27.886
This isn't normal!

01:28.053 --> 01:31.682
And I feel like these guys are even more
bloodthirsty now.

01:31.849 --> 01:34.852
Kotegawa definitely knows something about this.

01:35.436 --> 01:36.437
Hey, Chisa.

01:36.603 --> 01:37.855
What, Iori?

01:41.066 --> 01:42.735
I want to ask you something.

01:42.901 --> 01:43.902
Right now?

01:44.069 --> 01:47.239
We can talk in your room
after we go home.

01:49.658 --> 01:51.785
What's going on?
This is scary!

01:51.952 --> 01:54.788
Tell me! What's going on?

01:54.955 --> 01:56.790
I don't know anything.

01:56.957 --> 01:58.375
That can't be true!

01:58.542 --> 02:01.003
I have nothing to do with this.

02:03.922 --> 02:06.300
BREAK UP WITH CHISA KOTEGAWA,
OR WE'LL KILL YOU

02:06.467 --> 02:08.719
You have nothing to do with it?

02:08.886 --> 02:11.805
It says "Break up."
Are you guys dating?

02:11.972 --> 02:13.307
Of course not--

02:13.474 --> 02:15.309
From before the school festival.

02:16.643 --> 02:19.646
They'll kill you if you don't break up.
What will you do?

02:19.813 --> 02:21.690
I don't know.
I'll do what they say--

02:21.857 --> 02:25.944
Thanks, Iori!
You've decided to risk your life for me!

02:27.613 --> 02:29.490
What? What are you up to?

02:29.657 --> 02:32.659
Don't shout! You'll bother the others.

02:34.703 --> 02:37.706
-What's wrong, Kohei?
-Well, it's nothing big...

02:37.873 --> 02:40.918
-You mean this doesn't involve me?
-Yeah.

02:41.085 --> 02:43.545
We're just after that perverted bastard.

02:43.712 --> 02:44.922
I see.

02:45.547 --> 02:47.716
I just remembered I have something to do.

02:47.883 --> 02:49.718
Wait, Kohei!

02:49.885 --> 02:52.388
Don't talk to me!
They'll think we know each other!

02:52.554 --> 02:56.308
Know each other? We're best friends!

02:56.475 --> 02:59.353
Let me go!
This doesn't involve me!

02:59.520 --> 03:00.938
How can you say that?

03:01.605 --> 03:06.527
By the way, Kohei started dating Azusa Hamaoka from
OWU two weeks ago!

03:06.693 --> 03:07.694
Kitahara!

03:08.904 --> 03:13.617
Hey, you. Since you're my friend,
let's think about how to fix this situation together.

03:13.784 --> 03:15.661
Okay. You're right.

03:15.828 --> 03:17.496
I'm going to kill you someday.

03:18.205 --> 03:19.748
Anyway, Chisa--

03:19.915 --> 03:20.707
I'M GOING TO HAVE LUNCH CHISA

03:20.874 --> 03:21.917
She ran!

03:22.960 --> 03:26.797
Be passionate, my friends

03:26.964 --> 03:29.967
Shine bright with the sun

03:30.134 --> 03:33.512
Dive into the blue sky

03:33.720 --> 03:37.433
And let summer take it all

03:40.811 --> 03:44.398
GRAND BLUE DREAMING

03:51.697 --> 03:55.534
Be passionate, my friends

03:55.701 --> 03:58.787
Shine bright with the sun

03:58.954 --> 04:02.082
Dive into the blue sky

04:02.291 --> 04:06.336
And let summer take it all

04:06.503 --> 04:09.339
An expanding ocean of possibilities

04:09.506 --> 04:13.385
Summer is our amore

04:13.552 --> 04:17.055
We'll swear to the crystal clear sky

04:17.222 --> 04:20.184
Summer is in our hands

04:20.350 --> 04:24.271
Be passionate, my friends

04:24.438 --> 04:27.441
Shine bright with the sun

04:27.608 --> 04:30.903
Dive into the blue sky

04:31.111 --> 04:34.531
And let summer take it all

04:34.698 --> 04:38.702
With a cheerful heart

04:38.869 --> 04:41.705
Don't mess with me

04:41.872 --> 04:45.167
Keep going even if you fall

04:45.375 --> 04:49.004
And let summer take it all

04:54.134 --> 04:54.593
BREAKUP NOW

04:54.760 --> 04:57.471
I've never gotten so many letters before.

04:57.638 --> 05:00.682
Even guys from other departments sent some.

05:01.225 --> 05:02.726
What are you going to do?

05:02.893 --> 05:04.186
I don't know.

05:04.353 --> 05:07.231
Kitahara! Imamura! Got a minute?

05:07.397 --> 05:09.066
I'm Nojima, from your class.

05:09.233 --> 05:10.234
I'm Yamamoto.

05:10.400 --> 05:12.110
So who got the threat letter?

05:12.277 --> 05:13.821
Or is it for both of you?

05:13.987 --> 05:15.781
Are you already used to getting them?

05:15.948 --> 05:18.116
You guys aren't normal.

05:18.283 --> 05:19.910
You're in trouble, right?

05:20.077 --> 05:23.497
We're friends from the same department.
I wanted to help.

05:23.664 --> 05:24.665
Really?

05:24.831 --> 05:26.041
You guys are nice!

05:26.208 --> 05:28.835
But in return, I want you to teach me.

05:29.002 --> 05:30.087
Teach you what?

05:30.254 --> 05:31.630
I'm talking about that.

05:31.797 --> 05:36.093
How even a guy as perverted as you
can use hypnosis to get a girlfriend.

05:36.260 --> 05:37.261
You know how, right?

05:37.427 --> 05:38.595
Are you mocking me?

05:39.471 --> 05:40.472
You don't know!

05:40.639 --> 05:42.808
How is it possible you have a girlfriend?

05:42.975 --> 05:44.226
He's a total pervert!

05:44.393 --> 05:46.979
All of you, leave! Idiots!

05:47.479 --> 05:48.897
So you don't know?

05:49.064 --> 05:51.483
-Of course I don't know!
-I see.

05:52.109 --> 05:54.611
You guys! He doesn't know hypnosis.

05:54.778 --> 05:56.113
That's so disappointing.

05:57.447 --> 05:58.532
What's up with them?

05:58.699 --> 05:59.700
So, what do we do?

05:59.866 --> 06:02.619
The small mountain behind the clubrooms.
No one goes there.

06:02.786 --> 06:04.538
Right. Let's go there.

06:04.705 --> 06:07.249
Oh, no. They're talking about where to bury me.

06:07.416 --> 06:10.043
They found out you don't know hypnosis. That's it.

06:10.210 --> 06:11.461
Hey, Kitahara!

06:11.628 --> 06:14.089
Let's play hide-and-seek!

06:14.256 --> 06:16.049
Imamura, you too!

06:16.216 --> 06:17.509
No way! That's terrifying!

06:17.676 --> 06:18.927
Don't get me involved!

06:19.094 --> 06:21.930
Seeing that expression on your face is enough
reason for us!

06:22.097 --> 06:25.892
Listen, Kohei's not involved,
and you've made a mistake about me!

06:27.060 --> 06:28.270
Begging for your life?

06:28.437 --> 06:31.440
I've never heard anyone say
"begging for your life" before.

06:31.607 --> 06:34.901
Chisa and I, it's not what you're thinking!

06:35.068 --> 06:37.237
But you've been friends since childhood.

06:37.404 --> 06:39.239
At most, we're school friends.

06:39.406 --> 06:41.074
But you're together 24 hours a day.

06:41.241 --> 06:43.076
We're not dating!

06:43.243 --> 06:44.453
But you live together.

06:44.620 --> 06:46.788
Hey! Bring the shovel!

06:46.955 --> 06:49.166
-And the gloves and the towel!
-Yeah!

06:49.333 --> 06:52.544
You just wanted to save yourself.

06:55.547 --> 06:58.300
I'm telling you, it's not what you think!
Chisa and I--

06:58.467 --> 06:59.593
I got it. I got it.

06:59.760 --> 07:01.386
Tell us the details later.

07:01.553 --> 07:03.138
You're just saying that!

07:05.599 --> 07:09.978
She's the only girl in a department full of guys!
How dare you--

07:10.145 --> 07:13.565
And you're dating that cute girl from OWU, Imamura!

07:13.732 --> 07:16.318
Calm down. We can explain!

07:16.485 --> 07:18.320
Shut up and clench your teeth!

07:18.487 --> 07:20.656
If you kill us, it'll be at your expense!

07:20.822 --> 07:22.532
Begging for your life again?

07:22.699 --> 07:24.326
No... No! That's not--

07:24.493 --> 07:26.328
It's that--

07:26.495 --> 07:28.580
We'll plan a mixer for you!

07:28.747 --> 07:33.126
From now on, you're our best friends!

07:34.711 --> 07:36.338
So that's why...

07:36.505 --> 07:39.466
We want to ask Azusa to introduce us to her friends!

07:39.633 --> 07:41.218
What do you mean, "That's why"?

07:41.385 --> 07:43.595
You guys are always having fun.

07:43.762 --> 07:45.555
Well...

07:45.722 --> 07:46.723
Please!

07:46.890 --> 07:48.600
We thought you'd help us!

07:48.767 --> 07:50.268
Why don't you ask Chii-chan?

07:50.435 --> 07:51.561
That's...

07:53.730 --> 07:55.023
Chisa, please!

07:55.649 --> 07:57.567
Die 20,000 times.

07:57.734 --> 07:58.944
It's just like you said!

07:59.111 --> 08:01.947
She's been in a bad mood recently!

08:02.114 --> 08:03.490
It can't be helped.

08:03.657 --> 08:06.326
I'll introduce them, on one condition.

08:06.493 --> 08:07.494
Really?

08:07.661 --> 08:08.829
We'll do anything!

08:08.995 --> 08:10.789
Okay. Well, then...

08:11.456 --> 08:15.210
You have to act like you're Chii-chan's boyfriend
until Chii-chan accepts it.

08:15.377 --> 08:18.797
Azusa, why are you
adding that as a condition?

08:19.673 --> 08:21.341
I wonder why...

08:21.508 --> 08:22.592
What do you think?

08:22.759 --> 08:25.220
Well, if it'll save my life...

08:25.387 --> 08:26.430
Good!

08:26.596 --> 08:29.683
Then I'll bring a girl who's perfect for you guys.

08:30.600 --> 08:32.185
I'm back!

08:32.936 --> 08:33.937
Hey.

08:34.104 --> 08:35.480
Welcome back.

08:35.647 --> 08:36.690
So, Azusa...

08:36.857 --> 08:38.066
Where's your friend?

08:38.233 --> 08:39.860
Yeah. I brought her.

08:40.026 --> 08:41.445
Okay. Come in.

08:49.953 --> 08:50.954
Hi.

08:53.081 --> 08:55.500
What? What?

08:55.667 --> 08:56.877
She's amazing!

08:57.043 --> 08:59.463
-Thank you!
-You saved us!

08:59.629 --> 09:02.382
No big deal.

09:02.549 --> 09:05.093
Kohei! Bring some alcohol!
I mean tea!

09:05.260 --> 09:06.595
Do you like anime?

09:06.762 --> 09:09.139
Since she's here,
Does that mean she wants to join?

09:09.306 --> 09:11.391
How'd you find her
at this time of year?

09:11.558 --> 09:14.561
I didn't find her.

09:14.728 --> 09:16.938
Then who found her?

09:17.105 --> 09:19.399
It was Iori and the others.

09:23.069 --> 09:25.405
I'm Aina Yoshiwara,
a freshman at OWU.

09:25.572 --> 09:28.283
I'm quitting Tinkerbell
and joining Peek-a-Boo!

09:28.450 --> 09:29.451
Yoshiwara?

09:29.618 --> 09:30.786
Aina?

09:30.952 --> 09:33.038
-You're--?
-Cakey!

09:34.706 --> 09:36.374
Stop calling me that!

09:36.917 --> 09:39.252
-I see.
-So that's why.

09:39.419 --> 09:43.423
After the Izu Spring Festival,
she said she wanted to join our club.

09:43.590 --> 09:46.426
All right, Iori! Don't forget our promise, okay?

09:46.593 --> 09:48.345
No, this is a scam.

09:48.512 --> 09:50.722
It's just Cakey after she shed her skin!

09:50.889 --> 09:52.891
You guys are so rude!

10:00.106 --> 10:03.026
Anyway, nice to meet you.

10:03.193 --> 10:04.277
Yeah. Nice to meet you.

10:04.444 --> 10:05.904
Let's welcome her!

10:06.655 --> 10:07.656
Hey, Kohei.

10:07.823 --> 10:13.078
Yeah. Are we going to
have her set up the mixer?

10:13.245 --> 10:14.955
Grand Blue Dreaming

10:16.289 --> 10:17.582
The day has finally come.

10:17.749 --> 10:21.711
Do you think it's really okay to let Cakey--
I mean, Yoshiwara handle this?

10:21.878 --> 10:25.215
Hey! Thanks for waiting!

10:27.133 --> 10:30.470
So? Which school are the girls from?

10:30.637 --> 10:34.975
According to the girl who's introducing us,
they're all freshmen at OWU.

10:35.141 --> 10:37.060
OWU? Then they must be good!

10:37.602 --> 10:39.354
What's she like?

10:39.521 --> 10:41.940
Her? She wears a lot of makeup--

10:42.816 --> 10:46.361
Well, she's really different when she's serious
and when she's relaxing.

10:46.528 --> 10:49.364
-I see! I see!
-So she knows what she wants!

10:49.531 --> 10:52.617
She looked unhappy about it.

10:52.784 --> 10:56.079
Why was she so reluctant
to introduce her friends?

10:56.830 --> 11:00.125
It's not normal to ask a new member
to set up a mixer.

11:00.292 --> 11:03.086
-Please make an exception!
-You're saving our lives!

11:06.131 --> 11:07.757
You guys don't understand.

11:07.924 --> 11:09.426
Of course she wouldn't want to.

11:09.593 --> 11:10.635
Why?

11:10.802 --> 11:13.388
Introducing a pervert to your friends...

11:13.555 --> 11:16.141
I'd be too embarrassed to do it.

11:16.308 --> 11:18.643
Didn't you say we were best friends
the other day?

11:18.810 --> 11:21.646
You know you're going to a mixer
with us, right?

11:21.813 --> 11:25.233
You have a girlfriend!
Of course she doesn't want to introduce you!

11:25.400 --> 11:26.401
Right?

11:26.568 --> 11:29.905
No! Chisa's not--

11:30.071 --> 11:34.159
You have to act like you're Chii-chan's boyfriend
until Chii-chan accepts it.

11:34.326 --> 11:35.452
Chisa's not?

11:35.619 --> 11:38.246
Chisa is my girlfriend.

11:38.413 --> 11:39.623
Are you bragging?

11:39.789 --> 11:41.791
We'll throw you in the ocean, you idiot!

11:41.958 --> 11:44.544
Kitahara's job today is to help us get girlfriends.

11:44.711 --> 11:48.298
Since you already have a girlfriend,
it's natural.

11:48.465 --> 11:50.050
Hey. We're here.

11:50.216 --> 11:51.301
Here?

11:51.468 --> 11:52.469
Let's go!

11:52.636 --> 11:53.803
Wait!

11:53.970 --> 11:56.765
-Let's decide on a sign first.
-A sign?

11:56.932 --> 12:00.310
Yeah. We're going to point our chopsticks
towards the girl we like.

12:00.477 --> 12:03.146
-I see.
-It'll prevent fighting over girls.

12:03.313 --> 12:07.317
And if you don't like any of the girls,
the sign for "I give up"

12:07.484 --> 12:10.570
is pointing your chopsticks
towards yourself.

12:10.737 --> 12:12.197
That's a good idea.

12:12.364 --> 12:14.240
Your glasses are real.

12:14.407 --> 12:16.076
Quit joking around.

12:16.242 --> 12:17.243
Yamamoto?

12:17.410 --> 12:19.287
I don't need signs like that.

12:19.454 --> 12:20.705
But--

12:20.872 --> 12:24.084
I made a promise to myself.

12:24.250 --> 12:27.671
I don't care who it's with!
I'm going to lose my virginity!

12:27.837 --> 12:29.673
What a man.

12:29.839 --> 12:31.925
He's like some honorable soldier.

12:32.092 --> 12:34.719
He's just a piece of scum
who'd sleep with any girl.

12:34.886 --> 12:36.262
Are you ready?

12:36.429 --> 12:37.722
Yeah!

12:37.889 --> 12:40.225
We're going to a new world!

12:40.392 --> 12:42.686
Nice to meet you!

12:45.313 --> 12:47.482
Cakey! You bastard!

12:47.649 --> 12:49.317
Nice to meet you!

12:50.318 --> 12:51.319
No way!

12:51.486 --> 12:52.487
The girls are--

12:52.654 --> 12:54.614
Just give up for today!

12:54.781 --> 12:57.075
It's hot today, isn't it?

12:57.242 --> 12:59.244
-You're right.
-Let's have a toast!

12:59.411 --> 13:00.495
What do you want to drink?

13:00.662 --> 13:02.956
What should I have...?

13:06.418 --> 13:08.044
I'll start with some beer.

13:08.211 --> 13:09.212
Yamamoto!

13:09.379 --> 13:11.131
You're going to proceed?

13:11.297 --> 13:13.758
You're a stereotypical virgin!

13:13.925 --> 13:15.468
Cheers!

13:15.635 --> 13:18.263
-Let's introduce ourselves.
-Okay.

13:18.430 --> 13:20.265
I'll go first.

13:20.432 --> 13:22.726
I'm Kiyoko Kamio, a freshman at OWU.

13:22.892 --> 13:24.602
What are your hobbies?

13:26.730 --> 13:28.356
Horse racing and pachinko.

13:32.819 --> 13:33.820
Yamamoto!

13:33.987 --> 13:35.113
You want it that bad?

13:35.280 --> 13:37.407
I can't stop my tears!

13:37.574 --> 13:38.783
I'm Keiko Suzuki.

13:38.950 --> 13:40.326
I'm Kanako Iida.

13:40.493 --> 13:42.370
I'm Aina Yoshiwara.

13:44.581 --> 13:47.125
Hey, look how hard Yamamoto's trying.

13:47.292 --> 13:50.795
Yeah. We should at least make this exciting.

13:50.962 --> 13:53.298
He's acting so manly.

13:53.465 --> 13:55.508
I'm Iori Kitahara, a freshman at Izu U!

13:55.675 --> 13:56.926
I'm Kohei Imamura!

13:57.093 --> 13:58.303
I'm Hajime Nojima!

13:58.470 --> 14:00.055
I know it's still early, but...

14:00.221 --> 14:02.265
-I'm going to sit over here!
-I'm over here!

14:04.225 --> 14:06.061
You guys!

14:06.227 --> 14:08.313
Leave her to me.

14:08.480 --> 14:10.565
We're going to do our best to help you.

14:10.732 --> 14:12.567
We're praying for your success.

14:13.276 --> 14:15.570
I have good friends.

14:15.737 --> 14:16.905
This is for the best.

14:17.072 --> 14:19.574
The problem is what to do with this monster.

14:19.741 --> 14:22.077
Kitahara, what do you want to drink?

14:22.243 --> 14:24.120
You know how to do your job, right?

14:24.287 --> 14:25.288
Of course.

14:25.455 --> 14:27.832
We're going to make things fun and exciting!

14:27.999 --> 14:31.669
You look really different from the other day.

14:31.836 --> 14:32.879
Really?

14:33.046 --> 14:34.714
Oh, I see.

14:34.881 --> 14:36.049
How is she different?

14:36.216 --> 14:39.135
Her clothes and her makeup...

14:39.302 --> 14:41.346
She looks totally different.

14:41.513 --> 14:43.890
That's because this is a mixer.

14:44.057 --> 14:46.851
I put a lot of effort into getting ready.

14:47.018 --> 14:48.061
You hag!

14:48.228 --> 14:50.522
Get rid of some of that effort right now!

14:50.688 --> 14:53.108
The drinks are here, you two!

14:53.274 --> 14:54.651
You guys need to relax.

14:54.818 --> 14:57.737
Our job is to turn our brave friend into a man.

14:59.072 --> 15:00.865
You--?

15:01.032 --> 15:03.159
How can we help him?

15:03.326 --> 15:05.537
Let's get him to call her by her first name.

15:05.703 --> 15:07.580
You want to break the ice.

15:07.747 --> 15:08.748
Good idea.

15:08.915 --> 15:10.708
Here we go!
Stay with me, guys!

15:10.875 --> 15:11.876
Got it!

15:12.043 --> 15:13.378
Let's do this again!

15:13.545 --> 15:15.880
I'm Iori Kitahara.
You can call me Iori.

15:16.047 --> 15:18.883
I'm Hajime Nojima.
You can call me Hajime.

15:19.050 --> 15:20.760
You can call me Kohei.

15:20.927 --> 15:22.971
Then you can call me Kanako.

15:23.138 --> 15:25.223
My nickname is Kikko.

15:25.849 --> 15:27.142
I'm Shinichiro.

15:27.308 --> 15:28.434
Then you can call me--

15:28.601 --> 15:30.270
Hold on.

15:30.436 --> 15:31.813
What's wrong, Yoshiwara?

15:31.980 --> 15:33.189
You know...

15:33.356 --> 15:37.277
If we change what we call each other,
they'll get the wrong idea.

15:37.443 --> 15:39.362
Why is she saying that now?

15:39.529 --> 15:41.406
She messed up our plan!

15:41.573 --> 15:43.575
But, Kitaha--

15:43.741 --> 15:46.703
I mean, Iori.
If that's what you want...

15:46.870 --> 15:48.288
Not at all, you makeup maniac.

15:48.454 --> 15:51.124
Kitahara! We ordered a bottle!

15:51.291 --> 15:53.168
You drink a lot!

15:53.334 --> 15:55.628
Hey! Don't forget your job!

15:56.129 --> 15:57.130
You're right!

15:57.755 --> 15:59.883
This is all for our friend.

16:00.633 --> 16:02.177
I really...

16:02.343 --> 16:05.263
I really want to call you Aina.

16:05.430 --> 16:07.056
He did it!

16:07.223 --> 16:08.892
I see.

16:09.058 --> 16:11.060
You know, Iori...

16:11.227 --> 16:12.604
What?

16:12.770 --> 16:17.692
I couldn't hear you just now.
Can you say it again?

16:17.859 --> 16:19.194
Don't give in, Kitahara!

16:19.360 --> 16:22.030
You're heartless!

16:22.530 --> 16:25.074
Pardon my reach.
Here's your ramen salad.

16:25.241 --> 16:26.242
What's that?

16:26.409 --> 16:28.244
Haven't you heard of ramen salad?

16:28.411 --> 16:29.412
First time for me.

16:29.579 --> 16:31.039
Can I take a selfie?

16:33.249 --> 16:35.126
Kanako, you really like taking selfies.

16:35.293 --> 16:38.546
-What kind of selfies do you take?
-Like this.

16:39.172 --> 16:41.049
Kanako said she made this.

16:45.261 --> 16:48.598
This girl is pretty!

16:48.765 --> 16:50.600
That can't be true.

16:50.767 --> 16:52.936
You're right. That's impossible.

16:54.646 --> 16:57.565
So your hobby is taking photos?

16:57.732 --> 16:59.108
I like movies too.

16:59.275 --> 17:01.236
I like movies too!

17:01.402 --> 17:02.487
You guys...

17:02.654 --> 17:04.364
Movies are fun, right?

17:04.530 --> 17:05.782
Retreat, Nojima.

17:05.949 --> 17:07.700
Did you watch any movies recently?

17:07.867 --> 17:09.494
You can't have her, Kitahara.

17:09.661 --> 17:11.871
I watched Koi Moyo the other day.

17:12.038 --> 17:13.414
Hold on!

17:13.581 --> 17:15.041
I saw that movie too.

17:15.208 --> 17:17.627
He switched his target!

17:17.794 --> 17:18.795
Oh, that one!

17:18.962 --> 17:20.213
That was good!

17:20.380 --> 17:22.131
I know how you feel!

17:22.298 --> 17:24.634
This is stupid. She's just a 3D girl.

17:24.801 --> 17:27.387
We're not from the same dimension--

17:28.680 --> 17:30.265
What's this DVD?

17:30.431 --> 17:31.975
This anime changed my life!

17:32.141 --> 17:34.269
Monster Magic Girl Lalako!

17:34.435 --> 17:36.896
No way...

17:37.855 --> 17:38.940
Why?

17:39.107 --> 17:41.276
You like that movie?

17:41.442 --> 17:42.860
That explosion scene is great!

17:43.027 --> 17:44.654
No! The sinking scene was better!

17:44.821 --> 17:46.489
The scene where she jumps off!

17:46.656 --> 17:48.032
It's a love story...

17:48.199 --> 17:49.367
Hey, you.

17:49.534 --> 17:50.535
Yes?

17:50.702 --> 17:53.538
Do you want to come over to my place
after this?

17:53.705 --> 17:54.998
What?

17:55.164 --> 17:56.958
I have to go to the bathroom.

17:57.125 --> 17:58.793
-Me too!
-Me too!

17:58.960 --> 18:00.503
Me too!

18:03.214 --> 18:06.301
You guys! I thought you were helping me!

18:06.467 --> 18:07.802
Who said so?

18:07.969 --> 18:10.722
Don't complain!

18:10.888 --> 18:12.140
Calm down, you guys.

18:12.307 --> 18:13.308
Kitahara!

18:13.474 --> 18:15.602
We're friends, right?

18:15.768 --> 18:18.187
-But--
-Jealousy won't lead you anywhere.

18:18.354 --> 18:20.398
Teamwork is the key to victory.

18:20.565 --> 18:21.858
What are you talking about?

18:22.025 --> 18:23.943
Talking fancy won't get me a girlfriend!

18:24.110 --> 18:27.447
If one of us becomes friends,
we can do another mixer.

18:29.115 --> 18:31.534
Today's mixer is for tomorrow.

18:31.701 --> 18:33.328
-I see.
-Kitahara...

18:33.494 --> 18:35.747
Tomorrow's mixer
is for the day after that.

18:35.913 --> 18:37.540
You're right.

18:37.707 --> 18:38.750
Do you understand now?

18:38.916 --> 18:41.836
-Of course!
-Let's claim victory together!

18:42.003 --> 18:45.048
Let's show them our bond!

18:46.382 --> 18:48.051
I watched that drama too.

18:48.217 --> 18:50.553
Really? It was good, right?

18:51.220 --> 18:53.765
There must be a way to stop him
from stealing the show.

18:53.931 --> 18:56.809
I won't allow him to claim victory by himself.

18:57.602 --> 18:58.603
Imamura?

18:58.770 --> 19:01.564
Our bond can't have a show-stealer.

19:02.231 --> 19:03.941
In the name of justice,

19:04.108 --> 19:06.819
I'm going to dispel your anger and regret.

19:07.779 --> 19:08.863
Imamura...

19:09.030 --> 19:10.948
Hey, Kitahara.

19:11.115 --> 19:12.116
What, Kohei?

19:12.283 --> 19:14.619
I heard some gossip...

19:14.786 --> 19:18.081
Are you getting along with your girlfriend these days?

19:18.247 --> 19:19.624
You devil!

19:19.791 --> 19:20.792
You bastard!

19:20.958 --> 19:24.128
You broke a mixer taboo!

19:24.295 --> 19:27.215
What did you say, you piece of trash?

19:27.382 --> 19:30.051
Are you that jealous of my success?

19:30.218 --> 19:31.636
But we're a team.

19:31.803 --> 19:34.472
I have friends who support my success.

19:34.639 --> 19:37.016
No! They're all trash!

19:38.351 --> 19:41.813
I thought you had a girlfriend, Kitahara.

19:41.979 --> 19:44.607
I was one step away! Damn!

19:45.274 --> 19:48.486
The fun college life
with a girlfriend I dreamed about.

19:49.278 --> 19:51.489
Do I have to give up now?

19:52.615 --> 19:55.284
-I--
-Let's order desert!

19:55.451 --> 19:57.036
Oh, good idea!

19:57.203 --> 19:59.288
Hey! This guy has a girlfriend!

19:59.455 --> 20:01.749
Right! It's really important!

20:01.916 --> 20:03.793
They have ice cream and crepes.

20:03.960 --> 20:06.546
-What should I choose?
-I want a crepe!

20:06.712 --> 20:08.548
Then I'll have ice cream.

20:08.714 --> 20:10.007
No way!

20:10.174 --> 20:12.510
Are you helping me?

20:15.847 --> 20:16.889
Hold on!

20:17.056 --> 20:19.851
We won't be long.
About what we said just now--

20:20.017 --> 20:21.769
It doesn't matter.

20:21.936 --> 20:22.937
Don't say that!

20:23.104 --> 20:26.899
Aina already told me Iori has a girlfriend.

20:29.610 --> 20:31.446
MUMBO JUMBO

20:31.612 --> 20:34.157
Thanks for the meal!

20:35.908 --> 20:37.952
Nothing happened in the end.

20:38.119 --> 20:39.704
We were completely defeated.

20:39.871 --> 20:42.790
What a waste of time and money.

20:43.749 --> 20:45.084
What's wrong, Kitahara?

20:45.251 --> 20:47.211
Didn't you guys hear?

20:48.087 --> 20:49.464
What are you talking about?

20:49.630 --> 20:52.717
Those girls... The moment they turned around...

20:52.884 --> 20:54.302
That was fun!

20:54.469 --> 20:56.554
-That was great, right?
-Yeah.

20:56.721 --> 20:59.557
Yeah. That was really fun!

21:00.266 --> 21:02.602
It was like a zoo.

21:04.395 --> 21:07.106
-I see.
-A zoo?

21:07.273 --> 21:09.150
Don't mess around with us!

21:09.317 --> 21:10.443
Who is an animal here?

21:10.610 --> 21:12.862
Go look in the mirror first!

21:13.029 --> 21:16.157
You all look like clowns with your makeup!

21:16.324 --> 21:17.366
Let's go have a drink!

21:17.533 --> 21:18.534
Nice idea!

21:18.701 --> 21:20.286
Let's get out of here!

21:20.453 --> 21:22.830
I regret this! Damn!

21:25.041 --> 21:27.835
Hey, Aina.
Was that what you wanted?

21:28.628 --> 21:30.880
Sorry for asking you to do
something weird.

21:31.047 --> 21:34.383
It's okay. It was fun wearing makeup like that.

21:34.550 --> 21:37.136
You'll let us copy your report.

21:37.303 --> 21:39.180
But are you okay with this, Aina?

21:39.347 --> 21:40.640
What?

21:40.806 --> 21:44.810
There might have been someone good there.
But dressed up like that...

21:44.977 --> 21:48.147
It's okay. I've already shown them.

21:48.314 --> 21:50.733
Oh, you're talking about
the other day.

21:50.900 --> 21:54.111
They've seen you dressed like that.
You have nothing to be scared of!

21:54.278 --> 21:55.363
What?

21:56.239 --> 21:58.699
I know we're in no position to criticize you, but...

21:58.866 --> 22:00.243
Look at this photo!

22:01.536 --> 22:02.870
Send it to me!

22:03.412 --> 22:05.373
And...

22:05.957 --> 22:08.417
Pretty funny, right?

22:08.584 --> 22:13.256
Don't you think that a guy who's nice no matter how
you look is the guy for you?

22:14.674 --> 22:15.758
There you go again!

22:15.925 --> 22:18.511
You've been watching too many dramas.

22:19.220 --> 22:20.805
What?

22:20.972 --> 22:25.142
Kanako-chan would have said okay
if you guys hadn't gotten in the way!

22:25.309 --> 22:27.436
Don't be a sore loser, Kitahara!

22:27.603 --> 22:29.272
We're friends, right?

22:29.438 --> 22:31.941
I'll never forgive a traitor!

22:32.400 --> 22:33.776
DEEP BLUE AL FINE
KAYA MIZUKI

22:33.943 --> 22:36.028
Here's your mic, Kitahara.

22:36.195 --> 22:40.199
Me, too...? All right, let's do this!

22:40.408 --> 22:43.744
-Yeah, sing your heart out.
-You guys seem to be having fun.

22:45.371 --> 22:51.377
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.544 --> 22:57.300
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.466 --> 23:03.264
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:03.431 --> 23:09.562
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.729 --> 23:14.817
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.984 --> 23:22.408
Even if I were to lose everything
I'd still want you to know

23:22.575 --> 23:28.497
Trapped in the sky so far away
I'm praying with ripped off wings

23:28.706 --> 23:34.462
Because we span together
The vows of areppegio

23:34.629 --> 23:40.384
If life sparkles only to the beat
of the resonating stars

23:40.551 --> 23:43.387
I'll sacrifice everything

23:43.554 --> 23:47.933
Till death do us apart

23:48.142 --> 23:50.019
Cheers!

23:54.815 --> 23:57.443
Thank you!

24:02.490 --> 24:04.909
Iori, are you studying for your license?

24:05.993 --> 24:07.495
This feels like...

24:07.662 --> 24:10.039
Good things really do happen!

24:10.247 --> 24:11.582
By the way, Iori...

24:11.749 --> 24:12.833
Yes?

24:13.334 --> 24:16.003
I heard something just now.
Do you know anything about it?

24:16.185 --> 24:16.977
NEXT EPISODE
"FIRST BUDDY"
